                                       "kibana.alert.rule.parameters":  {
                                                                            "description":  "Detects wscript.exe, cscript.exe, or mshta.exe creating a powershell.exe, pwsh.exe,\nor cmd.exe child process.\n\nThis is a parent-child relationship rule rather than a string match. The child command\nline may be entirely innocuous, so no keyword would catch it; what makes the event\nsuspicious is who started it. Script hosts are a standard first stage for macro and\nscriptlet delivery, and they have very little legitimate reason to launch a shell on\na workstation.\n",
